            <ArticleTitle>Extended emergency care for painful conditions.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>233-8, ix</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Painful conditions are a common cause for visits to emergency departments. Appropriate therapy often consists of sedating medications followed by a period of observation that is beneficial in assessing their effect. The cause of abdominal pain is frequently elusive, requiring prolonged testing and re-examination. Observation is particularly beneficial in assessing this condition, while certain other painful conditions are not suitable for emergency observation because of the need for prolonged treatment.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
